Ubuntu
ArchLinux
Obsidian/workspace.json

# Personal config override - your machine-specific values (identity, paths, hostnames, ...),
# deep-merged over Configuration.psd1 at load time by Load-PathConfiguration. Written by
# Initialize-Configuration. Keep it on your machine / in your fork; never committed to WinuX.
# Match by filename (no leading path) so it is ignored wherever it lands - it holds a real Git
# identity and paths, and must never be published even if a stray/older copy sits in another dir.
Configuration.local.psd1

# Personal app-list overlays - exactly the same idea as Configuration.local.psd1, for the three
# app CSVs. Import-AppCsv layers <name>.local.csv over the committed <name>.csv at read time and
# Save-AppCsvOverlay writes it, so a fork's own app choices never touch a tracked file. WinuX
# ships only the base lists, so the overlays are ignored here. A fork that runs several machines
# can commit its own overlays (see docs/contributing/fork-model.md) - upstream never tracks them,
# so committing them downstream never conflicts on a pull.
Windows/PowerShell/Modules/Bootstrap/Data/*.local.csv

# LEGACY sidecar backups. The writers now back up into Backups/ instead, but older WinuX versions
# left these beside the files they protected, stale copies still sit on existing machines and in
# forks, and an AI assistant that cannot create directories still falls back to the .psd1.bak
# (see docs/reference/backups.md). They hold a real Git identity, so they must stay uncommittable.
Configuration.local.psd1.bak
Windows/PowerShell/Modules/Bootstrap/Data/*.local.csv.bak

# The unified backup sink - everything a WinuX writer replaces (files displaced by symlinks,
# rewritten configuration files, overwritten system files) is first copied by Backup-RepositoryItem
# into Backups/<OS>/<Category>/<Key>/<timestamp>/, one timestamped folder per replacement, bounded
# by Clear-OldBackups. OS-namespaced (Backups/Windows/ here) so a fork carrying other systems'
# tooling can give each its own sibling. Kept in the repository so a replaced profile or settings
# file is easy to find again, but it is your machine's own data (and may hold secrets), so it is
# never committed. See docs/reference/backups.md for the full policy.
Backups/*
!Backups/.gitkeep

# Logging module - generated logs (kept locally for inspection, never committed)
Windows/PowerShell/Modules/Logging/Logs/*
!Windows/PowerShell/Modules/Logging/Logs/.gitkeep
!Windows/PowerShell/Modules/Logging/Logs/Pinned/
Windows/PowerShell/Modules/Logging/Logs/Pinned/*
!Windows/PowerShell/Modules/Logging/Logs/Pinned/.gitkeep

# Tests module - generated run artifacts (merged run logs, per-worker NUnit XMLs, the measured
# per-file timings the harness buckets the next run with). Regenerated on every Run-Tests.
Windows/PowerShell/Modules/Tests/Results/*
!Windows/PowerShell/Modules/Tests/Results/.gitkeep

# Window module - per-machine runtime snapshot of the most recently applied workspace
# (written by Save-CurrentLayout, overwritten on every open). Machine-specific, never committed.
Windows/PowerShell/Modules/Window/Layouts/CurrentLayout.txt

# Workflow module - per-machine record of what each Open-Workspace invocation actually opened
# (written by Save-WorkspaceState, consumed by Close-Workspace). Describes windows that are open
# right now, so it is meaningless on another machine or in a later session. Never committed.
Windows/PowerShell/Modules/Workflow/State/*
!Windows/PowerShell/Modules/Workflow/State/.gitkeep

# WinuX.exe is a BUILD OUTPUT - compiled from WinuX.ps1 by New-WinuXExecutable.ps1 and attached
# to every tagged GitHub release by .github/workflows/release.yml. Never commit the binary;
# download it from <repo>/releases/latest/download/WinuX.exe instead.
Windows/WinuX/WinuX.exe